**Rule (Evidence statuses)** · `rule:design:evidence-status` A claim is planned, held, failed or passing with an execution artifact and its premises. Promotion to passing requires the exact supported input surface, profile and independent check to be named. Apply (`rule:testing:results`) to every minting and citing test: one failed sibling fails the claim; missing required executions keep it held. Evidence links obey (`rule:testing:coverage`). Skipped, incompatible and unexecuted cases remain visible and never contribute to a passing total. Later audit and commissioning report this supported surface rather than inferring readiness from repository cleanliness. Release support follows (`rule:compatibility:pre-one`). Observation follows (`rec:observe:decision`).

**Observation (Released reference evidence)** · `obs:design:reference-certificate` {% set reference = row('org.peer-network.design.constants', id='standing_profile').definition %}{{ require(reference.certified_strength == '1' and row('org.peer-network.design.constants', id='result.standing.width_lo').id != '' and row('org.peer-network.design.constants', id='result.standing.width_hi').id != '' and row('org.peer-network.design.constants', id='result.standing.fence_lo').id != '' and row('org.peer-network.design.constants', id='result.standing.fence_hi').id != '' and row('org.peer-network.design.constants', id='result.standing.fence_pass').id != '', 'reference evidence requires the published standing results and exact profile') }}The released result.standing width, evaluated fence and verdict describe the conserved reference equilibrium. The independent certificate ``ver:standing:conserved-equilibrium-enclosure`` establishes its coordinate enclosure and unique equilibrium throughout the contributing hull, with a separate local Krawczyk inclusion and certified final-set solvency, individual safety, admission and headroom. Its exact profile (`model:inventory:standing-profile`) passes at certified strength {{ reference.certified_strength }}; intermediate rungs are not inferred. The point-in-enclosure agreement in ``ver:standing:conserved-equilibrium-enclosure`` holds only for those exact Actor, vouch and profile inputs. Bite 6 transcribes that corpus and independently checks its residual and local-inclusion premises, centres and outward bounds; bite 7 checks its gates and bite 9 its replay. Different ledgers, depleted sources, deployment codecs and inter-epoch controller dynamics remain separate obligations. The retired staged verifier establishes none of these claims, and this released proof does not execute the implementation's held test-site claims.

