**Rule (Resource observation)** · `rule:design:observation-budgets` The work budgets of (`req:design:limits`) and (`rule:design:costs`) are deterministic computation inputs and counters, not sampled metrics. Mirror their consumed work and exhaustion class one way into metering under (`rec:observe:decision`). A sampled span cannot hide an increment from an enabled recorder, and a recorder's absence cannot grant more iterations or change INDECISIVE into PASS or FAIL. Wall time, allocation estimates, export backpressure and metric values never choose a rung or stop a binding refinement. Operational cancellation produces an incomplete run; it does not synthesize a mathematical verdict. Meter bytes, work units and inclusive duration for each operation, while excluding bounded observation buffers from binding work budgets and reporting their cost separately. Measurement for feasibility still requires (`expt:design:measurement-gate`), not an inference from trace presence.

**Rule (Storage observation)** · `rule:design:storage-observation` Trace the SCD2 operations of (`sig:design:storage`) under (`rec:observe:decision`) with child spans for as-of resolution and atomic successor/result transactions. Distinguish attempted succession, committed succession, rollback and retry; emit a committed outcome only after the database confirms commit, and an unknown outcome if acknowledgement is lost. Recovery resolves the durable event before retry accounting claims a new commit. Count durable changes separately from attempts, never infer a database commit from a trace, and reconstruct history from durable evidence when traces were lost. Record SQL statements, parameters, public row payloads, results and unsanitized driver errors in full under (`rule:observe:privacy`). Private instance settings, including the entire connection configuration, remain secret-typed and appear as role and marker. The storage adapter must establish (`inv:observe:secret-boundary`) through driver state and errors; an exposed connection value copied into an ordinary error fails admission rather than triggering sanitization. Effective boundary selection remains public-input semantics, not a timestamp read from observation. Names and stored-state evolution follow (`rule:compatibility:pre-one`).

**Invariant (Nonbinding diagnostics)** · `inv:design:observation-independence` Apply (`inv:observe:noninterference`) to every crate and external adapter under (`rec:observe:decision`). Record full verdicts, numeric witnesses, public payloads and backend errors under (`rule:observe:privacy`), with secret-typed instance material represented by role and marker. Metric failure attributes remain bounded for cardinality; traces carry complete detail. The authoritative witness remains in the publication or evidence artifact; a recorded copy supplies no extra mathematical authority. PASS, FAIL and INDECISIVE belong to the verdict algebra, while observation loss is an operational condition. Traces and metric snapshots never enter canonical encoding, semantic replay comparison, admission evidence or a claim of independent proof. Noninterference tests compare completed verdicts, standing and published bytes across disabled, full, filtered, sampled and failing-export configurations with identical public inputs and deterministic limits.

**Gate (Foundation observability bite)** · `gate:design:observability-foundation` {{ require(observation_foundation.before_bite == bites[0].ordinal and observation_foundation.packages == ['documents', 'pn-interchange', 'cli-common', 'execwrap'], 'observability foundation precedes the first adopted domain bite and covers the existing package roster') }}Complete an additional foundation bite before adopted bite {{ observation_foundation.before_bite | number }}: instrument {{ observation_foundation.packages | join(', ') }}, implement (`proposal:observe:enforcement`) and execute (`gate:observe:foundation`). Documents meters input projection, rendering and checks; interchange meters canonical coding, theory checks and acceptance without changing within-major laws; cli-common owns bootstrap, JSON sinks, operation guards and secret-typed observation; execwrap records full public child arguments, results and I/O without rewriting relayed bytes. Introduce the decided secrecy dependency (`dec:observe:secrets`) here, and replace content-exclusion paths with full recording and typed private inputs. Child inputs and outputs must obey (`inv:observe:secret-boundary`); a child that prints exposed secrets does not meet that contract. Owner: the foundation implementer and repository reviewer. Discharge accepted (`proposal:observe:export`) and prove its supported dependency set before integration; collector availability is never a gate dependency. Test with a local recorder and controlled exporter failures, secret-type compile-fail and runtime leakage probes, and full-public-content witnesses (`gate:observe:foundation`). This prerequisite does not renumber or reorder (`dec:decomposition:bites`); every subsequent domain bite enters already subject to the discipline. It is a required new foundation slice, not a claim that the current packages are fully instrumented. Trace and metric surfaces follow (`rule:compatibility:pre-one`). Observation follows (`rec:observe:decision`). Name and review the recorder-to-OpenTelemetry provider bridge, prove compatible versions and secret-typed exporter credentials. Record syntactically undecidable full-recording, secret-flow and ExposeSecret-consumer checks as reviewer-confirmed with negative probes, separately from mechanical coverage (`proposal:observe:enforcement`).

**Gate (Foundation claim bite)** · `gate:design:claim-foundation` {{ require(claim_foundation.before_bite == observation_foundation.before_bite and claim_foundation.packages == observation_foundation.packages and claim_foundation.status == 'held', 'claim and tracing work share the same held foundation bite and package roster') }}In the same prerequisite bite as (`gate:design:observability-foundation`), complete (`gate:testing:foundation`) for {{ claim_foundation.packages | join(', ') }}. Find test glosses that merely respell their function identifiers with spaces, rewrite them into reviewed statements of actual behavior and stakes, audit every current test site, and add or complete owner claim-area registers. Preserve existing claims where their statements remain valid; any renaming moves sibling and document citations in the same change (`rule:testing:evolution`). Implement (`proposal:testing:gate`), retain both already-active profiles and mint test-site claims for the new query's positive and negative probes. Replace this gate's held evidence links with those citations and recorded executions before closing the gloss-quality hold. Owner: the foundation implementer and repository reviewer. Domain owners activate both profiles and their registers at creation; the first domain crate is born traced and claim-tested. This is planned work, not evidence that the gloss-quality hold is closed. Complete the shared harness foundation (`gate:design:harness-foundation`) in this same prerequisite slice.

**Open Question (Observation implementation evidence)** · `open:design:observability-evidence` Owner: the foundation implementer and repository reviewer for the implementation conditions of accepted (`proposal:observe:export`) and (`proposal:observe:enforcement`). The discipline is accepted under (`rec:observe:decision`); its parsed coverage mechanism, reviewed dependency set, recorder/export integration, secret-boundary evidence and runtime independence evidence remain held until (`gate:design:observability-foundation`) passes. Any inability to instrument a public or generated entry point must use the checked item-local exception route rather than shrinking the census. Later domain coverage is an obligation of each owning bite, and loss-free telemetry or operational availability is not claimed by a mathematical verdict.

## Resources and performance · `sec:design:resources`

**Experiment (Declared workloads)** · `expt:design:workloads` Each implementation bite declares workloads by anchored Actors, accepted acts, complete projections, dependency incidence, sparse base nonzeros, supported horizon, integer bit length, precision and raw path-prefix count. Include isolated Actors, dense support, shared dependency ancestors, equal-width differently shaped graphs, depleted relays and adversarial signed cycles. Record input construction separately from solve, publication and replay; no measured throughput or deployment capacity is claimed here. Observation follows (`rec:observe:decision`). Each workload receives a benchmark case, declared measurement configuration and retained results under (`rule:harness:benchmarks`).

**Requirement (Limit declaration)** · `req:design:limits` A supported execution profile supplies finite limits for input bytes, object count, references, nesting, rational bits, matrix support, horizon, interval precision, primitive operations, iterations, witness bytes and raw prefixes. Preflight excess reports unsupported; exhaustion during certified refinement reports INDECISIVE with its counter, while incomplete structural enumeration reports resource exhaustion without a mathematical verdict. A host's local deadline cannot rewrite the published certification policy. Release support follows (`rule:compatibility:pre-one`). Observation follows (`rec:observe:decision`).

**Rule (Cost accounting)** · `rule:design:costs` Sparse support propagation charges work in horizon times base nonzeros, including construction of contributing extrema and retained diagonals; fence evaluation is then a separate scalar cost. A map application charges sparse hop products and precision-dependent arithmetic. Factorized publication avoids a dense expansion but must retain the complete emitted operator. Raw enumeration charges visited-set work and every depth-dependent prefix, including parallel projections; it has no general constant-factor traversal claim (``prop:scalability:standing-certificate-cost``, ``lem:epoch:double-cover-bfs-correctness``). Observation follows (`rec:observe:decision`).

**Experiment (Measurements before feasibility)** · `expt:design:measurement-gate` Before commissioning a workload profile, measure peak memory, wall time, operation counts, precision growth, evidence size and rejection behavior on the declared workload family. Record compiler, backend, platform and resource limits with the measurements. The performance risk (`warn:vision:performance`) remains held for feasibility until those measurements support a deployment budget; the semantic response to exhaustion is fixed here. Observation follows (`rec:observe:decision`). Comparable baseline and threshold declarations determine warnings and regression findings under (`rule:harness:benchmarks`), (`rule:devperf:comparison`); fast smoke runs cannot establish feasibility, and timing never fails a test, tier or gate.

